# VIGIL continuous re-proof — engagement config for vigil-reprove.service.
# Copy to ~/.config/vigil/reprove.env and edit. Leave VIGIL_REPROVE_ARGS
# UNQUOTED as a whole (systemd word-splits it into separate CLI args).
#
# The re-proof drives the SAME provenance-grounded finding `vigil remediate
# --prove` drives: a confirmed fact from the engagement's signed spine (or a
# signed, owner-delegated envelope), its retained firing oracle_context as the
# positive control, and the original exploit reconstructed from that retained
# material — re-fired against the live target each cadence.

# The writable engagement home (holds {slug}.spine, vault, the stable
# governance + self-witness keys, and the attestation-log/ directory). This is
# the ONLY path the hardened unit is allowed to write (ReadWritePaths).
VIGIL_BASE_DIR=%h/vigil/.vigil-live

# The reprove flags (finding source + live target + base dir). Example — a
# from-spine finding re-driven against a chartered loopback target:
VIGIL_REPROVE_ARGS=--from-spine my-engagement --target-base-url http://127.0.0.1:8080 --base-dir %h/vigil/.vigil-live

# Envelope (owner-delegated m-of-n) alternative instead of --from-spine:
# VIGIL_REPROVE_ARGS=--finding-envelope %h/vigil/finding.json --owner-pubkey <b64> --delegation %h/vigil/deleg.json --scope my-engagement --target-base-url http://127.0.0.1:8080 --base-dir %h/vigil/.vigil-live
